.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 235-235","id":"aa33c80502e7cedbfc58309e9db05e82e1944ab2a9179ffd6c7131e081fce5d6","intervals":[[193,193]],"path":"test/ops/review/address-pr.helpers.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Accept the published head in incrementing-commit fixtures."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"9754d0accafeb69ae106ccb266105883486ef2d5","body":"**Check the recipient on the successful recovery request.**\n\nIn `rerequest` mode, Lines 134-138 populate `reRequested` before the first request fails. This assertion then passes even if recovery requests another reviewer and clears `pending-rerequests.json`.\n\nCapture the recovery request separately. Assert that its successful payload includes `reviewers[]=octocat`. Do not use entries retained from the failed request.","id":"8022f0a54c5fc16e5c116f5498a26e9dc0e83bd1d5b7bf81f6ad9c98963909b9","intervals":[[316,316]],"path":"test/ops/review/addressRerequestPersist.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Check the recipient on the successful recovery request."}],"head":"66e01d5092e41ecdc2d1d14a6eadfcfad44eed8a","head_tree":"1ecd116c4ac33bbae984033dfd03894947e6454f","input_scope":[{"blob":"be942d8c69e67984527be1e128707542767866f3","intervals":[[1,1169]],"path":"test/ops/review/address-pr-git.helpers.ts"},{"blob":"70a8c4545ec989dfc8b22cb319c8e6864bffc219","intervals":[[1,684]],"path":"test/ops/review/address-pr.helpers.ts"},{"blob":"9754d0accafeb69ae106ccb266105883486ef2d5","intervals":[[1,330]],"path":"test/ops/review/addressRerequestPersist.test.ts"},{"blob":"9b0f1cf963df0a03bdc9436662afea4b9a5eaa21","intervals":[[1,510]],"path":"test/ops/review/addressWorker.isolationRefusals.test.ts"},{"blob":"37937ca55b7f05265e8fe79496a339a718096d93","intervals":[[1,544]],"path":"test/ops/review/findings.test.ts"},{"blob":"dccb4272e3d6f8a28eb6a715e68e34f44f01bce3","intervals":[[1,824]],"path":"test/ops/review/observation-wiring.test.ts"},{"blob":"dad54fd4e87